within ThermoSysPro.FlueGases;

package Machines "Machines"
  extends ThermoSysPro.UsersGuide.Documentation.ThermoSysProPackageIcon;
  annotation(Documentation(info = "## Copyright © EDF 2002 - 2025

## ThermoSysPro Version 4.2

Machines  


A gas turbine is a rotating device that converts the hot flue gases resulting from air compression and combustion with gas into mechanical energy.  
The gas turbine consists in a compressor and a combustion turbine.  
Several models of compressors and combustion turbines are available here.  

For a better understanding of the underlying physics, see Chap. 11 of :cite:`el19`.  



     

    "));
end Machines;